+--[ godmode ]-----------------------------------------------------------+
| version .. 0.6.1                                                      |
| source ... https://github.com/lofimichael/godmode-cli                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

  Godmode keeps the provider keys in .env.godmode and includes some notes
  on getting them. The file can be shared by your local agents. You don't
  have to run this program every time an agent needs a key.

[ installation ]

  Run install.sh without arguments. It selects a release for this machine,
  checks the download and starts setup. Private releases use your existing
  GitHub CLI login; see the one-command installation in README.md.
  Run godmodeup to fetch updates. It replaces only a managed executable;
  an unrelated or modified binary needs an explicit --force.

  New installs use ~/.godmode/bin/godmode, with keys and state under the
  same ~/.godmode home. Existing ~/.config/godmode setups are detected and
  left in place. No keys or rules are moved. The README install uses --path
  to add one shell entry; omit it to manage PATH yourself.

[ interactive setup ]

  Run godmode setup. Pick a provider by number or name, follow its links,
  and paste the credential when prompted. It is masked. Enter saves it;
  an empty prompt skips it. Existing values are kept unless you choose to
  replace them. Esc or Ctrl-C cancels the current input. No editor opens.
  Colors follow your terminal, with restrained accents; NO_COLOR opts out.

  godmode setup github goes straight to GitHub. The full-screen board is
  still available through godmode onboard, including its Picard controls.
  A fresh setup shows the warning before creating files; type GODMODE to
  acknowledge it. Browser links open only when you ask.

[ before adding keys ]

  A provider will accept whatever operations the key permits. It won't
  distinguish between a useful deployment and an agent misunderstanding
  which project you meant. Check the account and permissions before adding
  the key. You don't need to fill in every provider in the list.

  The file is plaintext, mode 0600. That keeps other ordinary users out;
  programs running as you can still read it. Godmode does not sandbox
  those programs or impose a spending limit. Saving a live key does not
  authorize charges or public actions.

  The run command passes only the keys you select, plus basic process
  context. Its output is not filtered. A child that prints its environment
  can therefore print those keys. Keep the file out of Git and bug reports.
  Revoke exposed keys at the provider; deleting the file won't revoke them.

[ picard ]

  godmode picard link     print the original YTMND URL
  godmode picard open     open it in a browser
  godmode picard show     show its image in the terminal
  godmode picard play     loop the original audio excerpt
  godmode picard stop     stop this state directory's player

  The board has i for the picture, p for audio and v for the original site.
  Picture and audio are separate requests. Nothing plays on startup.
  The first request downloads the relevant asset from YTMND into a local
  cache. Neither asset is included in this archive. Use the same --state-dir
  when stopping a player that was started with an override.

[ notes ]

  The lettering is original. The language and presentation sources are
  discussed in docs/CULTURE.md, including the Usenet post preserved at
  https://www.nongnu.org/ratpoison/inspiration.html .

  Picard: https://picard.ytmnd.com/ ; music by DarkMateria.
  This project's MIT license does not cover the source image or recording.

